{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-heat-equation-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-heat-equation-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence and uniqueness for the $q$-heat equation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-heat-equation"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-q-heat-equation-exists"],"tags":["existence","q-heat-equation","well-posedness"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QHeatEquation.exists_solution","text":"q-heat-equation-exists.md","leanSource":"q-heat-equation-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:q-heat-equation-exists\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, \\varTheta, G, \\mathcal{S})</code> be a quantum observable universe with initial data <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u_0 \\colon \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathbf{1}_{\\mathbf{C}}</code>. There exists a formal solution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u(t)</code> of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat equation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\partial_t u = -\\Delta_q u</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u(0) = u_0</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation-exists.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"4.21.3","page":"b/prop-q-heat-equation-exists","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":70},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.QHeatEquation.exists_solution","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation-exists.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
